@startuml
title udo — save(path): re-save the nearest file-owning container

actor TUI
participant Tree
participant Node
participant "persist\n(write_toml_atomic / AppConfig::save)" as Persist

TUI -> Tree : save(path)
Tree -> Tree : owner = nearest Container ancestor(path)
alt owner.kind == Global (root)
  Tree -> Node : to_app_config()\n(tasks = Task children,\n workspaces = Container child dirs)
  Tree -> Persist : AppConfig::save() -> config.toml
else Workspace / Project / nested
  Tree -> Node : to_container_data()\n(tasks = Task children,\n children = Container child dirs)
  Tree -> Persist : write <dir>/.udo.toml
end
Persist --> Tree : Ok
Tree --> TUI : Ok

note over Tree
  Editing a Task never writes its own file —
  it re-saves the parent container that owns it.
end note

@enduml
